From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] tapi32: line applications and devices for a machine without telephony hardware

lineInitialize, lineInitializeExA/W, lineShutdown, lineGetMessage,
lineNegotiateAPIVersion/ExtVersion, lineGetDevCaps/AddressCaps, lineOpen,
lineRegisterRequestRecipient/lineGetRequest, lineSetTollList, the device
configuration calls (lineConfigDialog*, line{Get,Set}DevConfig) and
lineGetIcon were stubs that returned success or garbage request ids.

They now keep a table of initialised applications under 32-bit handles,
honour the lineInitializeEx options (hidden window, event, completion
port) and version negotiation, and report zero devices, so everything that
names a device fails with LINEERR_BADDEVICEID (LINEMAPPER with
LINEERR_LINEMAPPERFAILED) after the usual handle and pointer checks. The
handles are written as 32-bit values as the Windows headers define them,
and the Ex parameter size is the packed one. The todo_wine marks in the
tapi32 test are gone.
---
